       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function and the absence of allergies don't change that.\n\nWas this a typo? Some possible intended doses:\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, a common starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, for frail patients or those who need a lower starting dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg is deliberate, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it."
