     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it, but 50 mg once daily is a dose I can't see a therapeutic reason for. It carries a real risk of serious harm, such as profound hypotension and shock. Amlodipine's long half-life of about 30 to 50 hours would also make that harm hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways I can help:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily**, the maximum labeled dose, if the goal is maximal amlodipine effect. If blood pressure still isn't controlled, adding a second agent is the usual next step.\n- **Enter a different dose** if 50 mg was a slip. Just give me the number.\n- **Flag the order for pharmacy review.** If you have a specialized reason for exceeding the labeled maximum, I'd suggest discussing it with the pharmacist or attending first and placing the order through the pharmacy-supported override process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
